{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different","id":1399266,"title":"How are the Abyss and the Lower Depths different?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-27T05:28:19-07:00","id":1399266,"title":"How are the Abyss and the Lower Depths different?","content":"Always had trouble with this one.<br /> <br /> Can Scelesti choose to be affiliated with either the Abyss or the Lower Depths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T05:39:50-07:00","id":1399270,"title":"","content":"To be Scelesti means to be associated with the Abyss. There's a bit more to it than just that, but a Scelestus associated with the Lower Depths is something that just doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T06:05:05-07:00","id":1399272,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26055\" data-vbnamecard=\"26055\">Krat05</a> thank you! That clears things up for me.<br /> <br /> Are there mages associated with the Lower Depths at all, or are they basically anathema to the Awakened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T06:06:11-07:00","id":1399273,"title":"","content":"Yes there are - Tremere most notably, but there's a couple of LD-aligned Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T06:12:14-07:00","id":1399274,"title":"","content":"So the Scelesti are aligned with the Abyss and the Tremere are aligned with the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> Thanks! That really helps.<br /> <br /> Duat, Inferno and Dis (the realm of the Strix) are Lower Depths, right? Would the Dark World from Princess: the Hopeful also be one if you included P:tH in your cosmology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T06:18:26-07:00","id":1399277,"title":"","content":"The Lower Depths are part of the Fallen World, and the Abyss isn't.<br /> <br /> The differences mostly pertain to origin lore and metaphysics. In practical terms there's not much difference between the two. For the purposes of Mage stories, they're both awful places that are home to reality-hating, pure evil monstrosities. In the context of telling a Mage story, it's entirely possible that the same story can work using the Abyss, a Lower Depth, or a particularly nasty Emanation Realm -- there's a lot of thematic overlap.<br /> <br /> I think the Lower Depths are included in the Mage cosmology largely as a hook-in point for crossovers with other splats like Mummy and Demon.<br /> <br /> Mage-specific content explicitly related to the Lower Depths comes mostly from Summoners I think, and there's also the lore for the Mage legacy Cwn Annwn. Even with the Tremere, their relationship to the Lower Depths is more like a rumor or a possibility that a ST can build on.<br /> <br /> I guess the signature gimmick of the Lower Depths in Mage is that it's devoid of mana and creatures from it really like eating mana, destroying parts of reality to convert them into mana, or similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-27-2020, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T10:27:16-07:00","id":1399313,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13121_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13121\" data-vbnamecard=\"13121\">galivet</a> thank you. I wonder if the Bound (giant Mana-eating monsters imprisoned by the Exarchs) are from the Lower Depths. Remind me again what an Emanation Realm is...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T10:45:48-07:00","id":1399316,"title":"","content":"As I understand it:<br /> The Abyss is Supernal Truth distorted, a Lie used by the Exarchs to maintain control over the Fallen World. The Abyss is the source of Paradox. It is only minimally under Exarch control, however, as Mythos-like world-gods, the Annunaki, float around the Abyss hungrily eating anything Supernal it comes across---INCLUDING the magic of even the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths, by comparison, are the further possible point away from the Supernal World, SO distant each Lower Depth (as there're a great number of these places) lacks some vital part of existence. Known Lower Deptjs include Duat and the shadowy forest-world the Strix come from.<br /> <br /> Mages can journey into either, though, unless you're an archmaster, the trip is going to be one way only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T10:57:28-07:00","id":1399318,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12219\" data-vbnamecard=\"12219\">Demigod Beast</a> thanks. That\u2019s really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T12:45:47-07:00","id":1399353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399313#post1399313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13121_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13121\" data-vbnamecard=\"13121\">galivet</a> thank you. I wonder if the Bound (giant Mana-eating monsters imprisoned by the Exarchs) are from the Lower Depths. Remind me again what an Emanation Realm is...?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bound are <i>Supernal</i> entities in exile. They eat Mana not because Mana is inherently lacking from their origin but because they are supposed to be in &quot;Mana-rich environments&quot;, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I actually didn't know that Mana was supposed to be missing from the Lower Depths, although it would make sense. But the main focus of the Lower Depths is that each one lacks (and thus in some way consumes) an aspect of reality. Duat lacks Sekhem, a type of life energy. Strix-world is theorised to also lack life-energy, but in the form of Vitae. The Inferno lacks Virtue which they &quot;consume&quot; by spreading Vice in the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-27-2020, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T13:49:07-07:00","id":1399368,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> awesome. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T17:01:34-07:00","id":1399429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duat might or might not be though given the categorization mages use that is more an academic thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also confirmed by the devs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T17:02:47-07:00","id":1399430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399273#post1399273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes there are - Tremere most notably, but there's a couple of LD-aligned Legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are legacies connected to power depths inherently Left Handed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T17:17:53-07:00","id":1399433,"title":"","content":"Duat isn\u2019t a clear cut case. It might be associated with Lower Depths, it may be more Abyssal. Or it may be something else entirely, empowered by the Rite of Return that broke the world as it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T18:06:46-07:00","id":1399446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399433#post1399433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duat isn\u2019t a clear cut case. It might be associated with Lower Depths, it may be more Abyssal. Or it may be something else entirely, empowered by the Rite of Return that broke the world as it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I thought all other realms besides the supernal/abyss/Shadow/astral were considered Lower Depths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T19:44:21-07:00","id":1399471,"title":"","content":"Also, for entities from there, keep in mind creatures from the Lower Depth want to steal or experience what they lack, and have pretty understandable minds; fiends of Duat want to torture people because it makes them hurt less, Strix steal bodies because otherwise they have no Life to experience physical existence or sensation with.<br /> <br /> Abyssal beings either hate the world or cannot adapt it to fit them, so they destroy things out of hand, either intentionally or due to their natures crashing with it. They're often extremely alien and often arguably not sentient in any meaningful way. <br /> <br /> A good rule of thumb is that a Lower Depths demon is incomplete and seeing completion, an Abyssal gulmoth is an oxymoron in some way, and that paradox damages everything nearby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T19:50:38-07:00","id":1399474,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> Paradox is an Abyssal phenomenon, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T19:56:06-07:00","id":1399476,"title":"","content":"Emanations are essentially the foundations for alternative settings for Mage. They're planes of existence situated between the Material and the Supernal. Each is themed according to a particular Aracanum and symbol set. You get to one through a special kind of Iris. Signs of Sorcery explains them in detail, but the bottom line is that if you want to play Mage in some tropey alternative reality like Dinosaur World, Post Apocalyptic Urban Decay, Water World, or Burning Hellscape you can situate it in an Emanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T20:00:49-07:00","id":1399478,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13121_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13121\" data-vbnamecard=\"13121\">galivet</a> nice!!! Maybe I will pick up Signs of Sorcery after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T05:50:03-07:00","id":1399577,"title":"","content":"In 1e, specifically Inferno, they make the distinction that the Abyss can be viewed anti-reality and ultimately wants to annihilate the world, subsuming it piece by piece. Off-hand I don't recall if the Abyss is doing the same to the Lower Depths, but at least Inferno actually love (in-so-far as they are able) the world as it is. The Abyss is destroying what Inferno seeks to claim for its own, and there is a brief sidebar describing how the two realms occasionally clash in open battle. In short, the Abyss wants to devour what Inferno seeks to corrupt, and the two goals are mutually exclusive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24688-mrmeow","name":"MrMeow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T06:03:41-07:00","id":1399578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399446#post1399446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. I thought all other realms besides the supernal/abyss/Shadow/astral were considered Lower Depths?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a bit more complicated than that, but still not a bad way to go, IMO.<br /> <br /> The first thing we need to remember that the Lower Depths is something that mages ue to describe some realms of existence. The fact that mages would call a certain realm a &quot;Depth&quot;, does not immediatly means anything that those realms share in common, beside the fact that those realms lack some aspect of themselves, and that they devour that aspect from the material world. Depths have almost nothing in common, and mages simply group them together because that's what mages do- but again, if you were to have some realm that is not based around lacking a certain aspect of reality and eating that aspect in some way or form, it is not a Depth, but something else which is found outside of Mage's cosmology all together.<br /> <br /> Now, the thing is that when you examine Mage's most basic definition for a Depth, Duat does checks out- it is a world outside of the overall model, which lacks some aspect (Sekhem/ Souls) and which devours that aspect from reality. Ammut, as a being of hunger, fits those themes, and a mage who would discover the Arisen and their cosmology is likely to claim it to be a Depth without a second thought. On the other hand, Duat does seems to be more &quot;special&quot;- as many of the Depths are &quot;just&quot; dark corners of existence while Duat seems to be related to the primordial concepts of souls and creation. If it is what the Arisen claim it to be, it is a realm where all souls are being judged, where the worthy should gain access to A'aru, whatever that means and wherever it may be. But then again, who said that mages would not lump realms of great importance as a part of the Lower Depths just because they are important? No one ever said that Depths can't be important- Inferno is such example, and Dis is also a world we shouldn't disrespect. <br /> <br /> So in short, the Lower Depths ia a term which mages use to describe many realm which do not fit to their model, and which all lack a certain &quot;thing&quot;. It is an in character term, which of course puts the Supernal in the middle and the Depths at the periphery because that is Mage's ciosmology model. Are those realms indeed perepherial? Are all the realms that mages call &quot;Depths&quot; are indeed just the same? How much of Inferno, Dis and Duat share with one another beside all lacking something? That's the thing- Mage's model only has one dimension: moving from the top to the bottom. What about going sidewise? How many dimensions do we really need in order to truly decribe the multiverse? <br /> <br /> That leads me back to the main topic of this thread- the difference between the Lower Depths and the Abyss. On the surface, the two of those do have something in common- they are antagonistic towards existence as we know it, and they both could contain countless of different realms and subrealms. However, there is a key difference between the two- the Abyss hates us, and the Depths love us. The reason is that the Abyss is about replacing aspects of our existence, while the Depths want to preserve the world as is- only make it worse, and worse, and worse. The reason is that the Depths eat parts of the world, and if the Abyss were to replace them, it would interfear with their nourishment. For example, what do you think would happen if the Abyss would replace all of the blood in the world with acid? Vampires will have to adapt to it, or go extinct. Vampires going extinct means that whatever gods which rule over vampirism would also die out. And as such, those blood gods would do everything they can in order to stop the Abyss from replacing blood with acid, because that's the existence they need in order to survive. A better - and canon - example would be the concept of the Abyssal Virtue, where the Abyss replaces what people have as Virtues with some other twisted morals. Inferno feeds upon Virtue. It is defined around corrupting Virtue. If you were to replace Virtue with something else, Inferno is no longer defined, its testaments mean nothing and it can no longer feed. As such, Inferno would fight any attempt of the Abyss to replace Virtue.<br /> <br /> So here is the main difference between the two- the Depths are tied to the world. They are what the world lacks, and as such they need it in order to feed. The Abyss, however, is what this world is not- it is defined by not being this reality. Everything which never was is found in the Abyss- and as the number of things which do not exist in inifnite and the number of things which do exist is finite, we are talking a vast realm of none existence, endless possibilities for how this world could be not what it is. The goal of the Abyss is to replace existence with all other existences- which means to destroy the world, for if all possibilities are ture, none are ture, and we are found in the Abyss. The Depths, however, wants to have to world to survive as is as long as possible, and remain in constant suffering, pain and decay. If the Depths are zeros, the Abyss is infinity. Try to multiply them together and all hell breaks loose- literaly. That's actually why I highly doubt that Duat is Abyssal in nature- it does not try to replace anything, does not represents any alternative reality, and wants to preserve the world as much as possible so it would suffer as much as poissible to feed it as much as possible. The Ocean of Osiris, however? Yeah, that may very well be the Abyss.<br /> <br /> To sum it up- the Lower Depths is a Mage term to describe things which Mages don't really understand, but they do have common traits (that is, lacking something about the world). The Depths differ from the Abyss because they love our world, seek to preserve it as much as possible and feed upon its misery, while the Abyss hates the world, seeks to end it as soon as possible and just wants silence. It is very likely that mages would call Duat a Lower Depth, but the fact that they do means practically nothing about whether it is true or how significant Duat is to the world, because their model only has one axis and is known to fail when you look sidewise. <br /> <br /> Just my view on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:11:45-07:00","id":1399588,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> I had a tangential question.<br /> <br /> Assuming Duat is in fact one of the Lower Depths, what is the relationship between Ammut the Devourer and the Judges of Duat?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m asking you specifically because you seem to know a lot about M:tC, but anybody can answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:15:48-07:00","id":1399589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1119539-a-possibly-rather-stupid-question-concerning-duat?p=1119569#post1119569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the slightest bit ambiguous. Duat is <i>not</i> in the Underworld. It <i>is</i> a Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though flip-flopping on such subjects is not unheard of (see vampires having souls and/or Oneiroi).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:20:12-07:00","id":1399590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399589#post1399589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though flip-flopping on such subjects is not unheard of (see vampires having souls and/or Oneiroi).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> thanks. I finally get it. I guess I was confusing Chronicles of Darkness with WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:31:16-07:00","id":1399591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399588#post1399588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> I had a tangential question.<br /> <br /> Assuming Duat is in fact one of the Lower Depths, what is the relationship between Ammut the Devourer and the Judges of Duat?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m asking you specifically because you seem to know a lot about M:tC, but anybody can answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact relationships between the two can be found in the Dreams of Avarice, where the Iremite creation story is being detailed- that is, if you want to take that myth as literal, which could be correct but who knows? Ay any case, the Judges seems to be from Duat but not of Duat. Ammut is an earlier entity, and the Judges exist in order to dictate what belongs to the Devourer and what is worthy for slavation. Perhaps Duat could be seen as the liminal place between the gult of the Devourer (which is the Lower Depth) and A'aru (which seems to be around the Supernal/ Empyrean level of reality), and the Judges are that boundary between doom and ascension.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the Judges exist as a compromise between the forces of destruction and the forces of creation, between entropy and enthalpy. The Judges feed Ammut because entropy must rise- or entropy rises because Ammut must be fed? Without the Judges, everything is doomed to the Devourer. Because of the Judges, almost everything is doomed to the Devourer. They are not the Devourer's underlings- but they also serve her, because it is easier, and less dangerous for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:34:59-07:00","id":1399592,"title":"","content":"@Lost Light perfect. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:35:43-07:00","id":1399593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399474#post1399474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> Paradox is an Abyssal phenomenon, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. Paradox and the Abyss are in many ways one and the same. Paradox is powered by the Abyss, and the fact that the Abyss cannot be true means that a lot of it has inherent Paradoxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T20:38:21-07:00","id":1400623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1399353#post1399353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Inferno lacks Virtue which they &quot;consume&quot; by spreading Vice in the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out that this is an inference based on the &quot;world without X&quot; descriptive model that doesn't quite bear out from how the Inferno operates. Virtue and Vice alone are not morally weighted, and Inferno makes distinctions between, for example, a goetic demon and a goetia that is an Infernal demon.<br /> <br /> A more concrete way of putting it is that, back on the old forums, Malcolm Sheppard once answered the question of why the Inferno was a Lower Depth with (slightly paraphrased) &quot;It's because evil is a lack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fast forward a couple years to the Mage 2e open development blogs, where this tidbit comes up in the discussion of the Paths' relation to morality:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/254357-fwc-weekly-discussion-death-is-the-road-to-awe?p=254531#post254531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my mind, evil is really about cultivating a lack of compassion within yourself--it's not a force coequal with good, a part of a cycle, or anything that balances anything else. It's not black on the chessboard. It's spitting in the other guy's face when you play, and smashing his king with a hammer instead of losing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appropriately enough, there's bits of this in Mummy, which Malcolm also contributed substantially to; Dreams of Avarice's distinction between the Self and the Will, as well as its illustration of how the Law of Suffering locks people into deliberate cruelty out of fear for their own comfort and well-being, bears mentioning when one looks at how the agendas of Infernal Dominions tend to break down \u2014 not for nothing do the two least-complicated categories of true demonic behaviors boil down to &quot;make the world materially worse to live in&quot; and &quot;kill people to hurt other people.&quot;<br /> <br /> The <i>akathartoi</i> warm themselves in the Inferno by getting people to forsake that crucial bit of sympathy for others. One of the key ways the Supernal differs from the Phenomenal World is that classical basis for compassion: all things are one, and separation is an illusion that leads us to hurt ourselves when we hurt others \u2014 moreso still when we double down on the idea that this is not the case and revel in having power over other people. Whatever the Judges truly are, they have a certain investment in propagating that form of evil at the very foundations of human civilization as they consume the stuff of manifest existence through their Arisen servants.<br /> <br /> (This got rambly, for which I apologize.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T21:25:20-07:00","id":1400626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1399266-how-are-the-abyss-and-the-lower-depths-different?p=1400623#post1400623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out that this is an inference based on the &quot;world without X&quot; descriptive model that doesn't quite bear out from how the Inferno operates. Virtue and Vice alone are not morally weighted, and Inferno makes distinctions between, for example, a goetic demon and a goetia that is an Infernal demon.<br /> <br /> A more concrete way of putting it is that, back on the old forums, Malcolm Sheppard once answered the question of why the Inferno was a Lower Depth with (slightly paraphrased) &quot;It's because evil is a lack.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fast forward a couple years to the Mage 2e open development blogs, where this tidbit comes up in the discussion of the Paths' relation to morality:<br /> <br /> <br /> Appropriately enough, there's bits of this in Mummy, which Malcolm also contributed substantially to; Dreams of Avarice's distinction between the Self and the Will, as well as its illustration of how the Law of Suffering locks people into deliberate cruelty out of fear for their own comfort and well-being, bears mentioning when one looks at how the agendas of Infernal Dominions tend to break down \u2014 not for nothing do the two least-complicated categories of true demonic behaviors boil down to &quot;make the world materially worse to live in&quot; and &quot;kill people to hurt other people.&quot;<br /> <br /> The <i>akathartoi</i> warm themselves in the Inferno by getting people to forsake that crucial bit of sympathy for others. One of the key ways the Supernal differs from the Phenomenal World is that classical basis for compassion: all things are one, and separation is an illusion that leads us to hurt ourselves when we hurt others \u2014 moreso still when we double down on the idea that this is not the case and revel in having power over other people. Whatever the Judges truly are, they have a certain investment in propagating that form of evil at the very foundations of human civilization as they consume the stuff of manifest existence through their Arisen servants.<br /> <br /> (This got rambly, for which I apologize.)</div> </div> </div> </div><i>THIS</i> is rambly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T21:44:55-07:00","id":1400630,"title":"","content":"I think the Cwn Annwn are one of the other Lower Depth-oriented legacies. They're considered left-handed and in the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Left-Hand_Path\" target=\"_blank\">Left-Hand Path</a> book. The legacy's creator found 'an in-between place, a void which was not the Abyss but could be filled by the energies of the Fallen World if an explorer was talented enough at giving form to Mana.' And the legacy seems to be mostly about turning that void into a paradise with the help of their new buddy, for 'Every member of the Legacy is host to a being of the Lower Depths.'<br /> <br /> It is one of the mage-confined ones that as far as I can tell has no intersection with other gamelines or books and is pretty clear on what it lacks and how it imposes itself on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-03-2020, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T10:03:39-07:00","id":1400770,"title":"","content":"Annwn is indeed one 